ook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>An image recording process which comprises printing a deep yellow portion with an ink composition comprising C.I Pigment Yellow 74 and printing a light yellow portion with a second yellow ink composition comprising at least one yellow pigment selected from the group consisting of C.I Pigment Yellow 109, 110, 128, 150 and 154. The use of a yellow ink comprising C.I Pigment Yellow 74 and the above second yellow ink in combination with each other as defined above according to the depth of color of a yellow image to be printed results in a significant improvement of the light fastness and coloring property of the yellow image.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Selon ce procédé d'impression d'image, on utilise pour les jaunes intenses une première composition d'encres à base de pigment jaune de type C.I Pigment Yellow 74, alors que pour les jaunes clairs on utilise une seconde composition d'encres à base de l'un au moins des pigments jaunes des types C.I Pigment Yellow 108, 110, 128, 150 et 154. L'utilisation d'une combinaison entre la première et la seconde des compositions d'encre en fonction de l'intensité et de la clarté du jaune dans l'image à imprimer permet d'améliorer sensiblement d'une part la tenue à la lumière et d'autre part la qualité chromatique du jaune dans l'image.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>